  "description": "qou-ales step 11: extends step 10's exact H_6 convention-D response computation to all four ORDERED two-nucleon channels and to all four gamma-gamma vertices at the interface. FINDING 1 (arity): at the canonical vertex V1 = sigma_2 sigma_3^-1 the response r is a function of the RIGHT nucleon ALONE -- r_pp = r_np and r_nn = r_pn exactly, r_pp != r_nn -- because a gamma-gamma vertex needs two adjacent generators and so must BORROW one from a nucleon; it sees only the one it borrows from. So it cannot distinguish a like pair from an unlike one, which is an ARITY obstruction to the sign-mixed two-body pattern qou-q8vl requires, stronger than a sign objection. FINDING 2: moving the borrowed generator to the other nucleon REVERSES the binding sign (V1 unbinds the deuteron by 4.469 keV; V3 = sigma_1 sigma_2^-1 BINDS it by ~57 keV, 13x larger), so the 'unbound' reading carried by steps 8-10 is scope-(a) -- true of V1 and reversed by the equally underived V3. FINDING 3: c_N carries one more factor (q^2-1) than c_P, so at V1 the dineutron deviates at h^5 against the diproton's h^4. Step 10's closed form and Lean are unaffected; what narrows is the interpretation. By-product: a fourth confirmation of qou-sikd. No AME/CODATA binding value or census read.",
